CASE ID: issue-related-pagination-not-duplicate
FLOW: issue triage
TRUSTED POLICY: Duplicate means the same root failure and requested outcome, not merely the same subsystem.
ISSUE #503
Title: Event client sends continuation under pageToken
Body: In 2.9.0, call buildListEventsRequest({cursor:'after:event/42', limit:25}). Expected: the URL contains cursor=after%3Aevent%2F42. Actual: cursor is absent and pageToken contains the value, so page two repeats page one. The public server accepts only cursor.
CURRENT SOURCE:
export function buildListEventsRequest({ cursor, limit }) {
  const url = new URL('https://events.invalid/v1/events');
  url.searchParams.set('limit', String(limit));
  if (cursor) url.searchParams.set('pageToken', cursor);
  return url;
}
DUPLICATE CANDIDATES:
- #94 Event inventory silently stops after ten full 100-item pages. The client sends the correct cursor on every request, but a local 1,000-item safety cap returns partial data instead of failing closed. Requested outcome: detect an incomplete full final page and abort.
- #95 Event request rejects limits above 100. Requested outcome: document the supported maximum.
SPECIALIST EVIDENCE: The supplied call deterministically demonstrates the wrong query key. #94 concerns completeness after many otherwise-correct cursor requests; #95 concerns input validation. Neither would be fixed by serializing cursor under the public key.

