CASE ID: review-stale-head-publication
FLOW: pull request review
TRUSTED COMPARISON: base212...head212, complete.
INVARIANT: Publication must use the exact frozen head after revalidating that the PR still points to it. The earlier pull snapshot may be stale independently of the final fresh snapshot.
DIFF src/publish.mjs:
@@
 export async function publishReview({ github, pull, frozenHead, body }) {
+  const fresh = await github.getPull(pull.number);
+  if (fresh.head.sha !== frozenHead) throw new Error('head moved');
   await github.createReview({
     pull_number: pull.number,
-    commit_id: frozenHead,
+    commit_id: pull.head.sha,
     body,
   });
 }
DETERMINISTIC REPRODUCTION: Invoke with an earlier pull snapshot whose head is old000, frozenHead=new111, and getPull() returning new111. Revalidation passes, but createReview receives old000. The base version sends new111.
NEARBY EVIDENCE: github.createReview rejects a commit that is not in the PR, but old000 remains in its history and is accepted, so server validation does not restore current-head authority.
Use finding key src/publish.mjs:12 for a current defect on the changed commit_id line.

