CASE ID: fix-expiry-equality-boundary
FLOW: controlled fix
EDIT BOUNDARY: src/expiring-cache.mjs and its test only.
PROVEN CONTRACT: A value is readable when now equals expiresAt and expires only afterward. The failing equality test sets at 1000 with TTL 500, expects the value at 1500, and expects undefined at 1501.
CURRENT SOURCE:
get(key, now) {
  const entry = this.entries.get(key);
  if (!entry) return undefined;
  if (entry.expiresAt <= now) {
    this.entries.delete(key);
    return undefined;
  }
  return entry.value;
}
PATCH OPTIONS:
A. Keep `entry.expiresAt <= now` and change the test to expect eviction at equality.
B. Change the condition to `entry.expiresAt < now`; retain both equality and after-boundary assertions.
C. Change the condition to `entry.expiresAt >= now`; retain the tests.
D. Make no change because boundary behavior is subjective.
Choose the smallest complete option that preserves the proven contract.

CASE ID: fix-concurrent-reservation-atomicity
FLOW: controlled fix
EDIT BOUNDARY: src/reservations.mjs and its test.
PROVEN CONTRACT: For overlapping reserve(key) calls, exactly one call may invoke persist and return true. A failed persist must allow a later retry. Different keys should not block each other.
CURRENT SOURCE:
class Reservations {
  #reserved = new Set();
  async reserve(key, persist) {
    if (this.#reserved.has(key)) return false;
    await persist(key);
    this.#reserved.add(key);
    return true;
  }
}
FAILING REPRODUCTION: Two calls for the same key both pass the check, both enter persist, and return [true,true].
PATCH OPTIONS:
A. Add a per-instance `#pending` Set. Reject when key is reserved or pending. Add key to pending before await; on success add it to reserved; always remove it from pending in finally. Test overlap, failed-persist retry, and independent keys.
B. Add key to reserved only after await, then check whether another call added it and return false for the loser.
C. Add key to reserved before await and never remove it if persist throws.
D. Serialize every key through one global promise chain and return true to all callers after the first persist completes.
Choose the smallest complete option.
